import { urls } from "../../../../data";
<div id="button-link-overview">
  <component-banner-img/>

  <p>
    A button link <em>looks</em> like a normal
    <a href=`${urls.components}/link`>link</a> , but is actually a button. Use a
    button link when the action triggers JavaScript behaviour (e.g. opening a
    dialog) rather than navigating to a URL.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because a button link is a real <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> element, it
    retains native keyboard and screen reader support for buttons, which would
    be lost if an anchor tag without an <code>href</code> were styled to look
    like a link instead.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <code>fake-link</code> class is deprecated and will be removed in the
    next major version of Skin. Use <code>button-link</code> instead.
  </p>
</div>
